[
  "Profile: Gal (age 6) communicates via AAC and strongly prefers interactive apps (drawing, music) over passive activities. Core interests: facts, drawing, music, and science—especially hands-on exploration (experiments, how things work, chemistry, weather), farm games, space topics (stars, moon, planets, rockets, astronauts), and programming (Code blocks, Games, Robots). Learning style: prefers hands-on, practical engagement and browses multiple options before committing to extended activities.",
  "Communication Style: Uses 'I'm thinking about' button to initiate guessing mode, preferring shorter, focused interactions with clear exit strategies. Typically looks down and to the side during communication—this is normal. When engagement seems uncertain, offer direct activity suggestions (e.g., 'Want to draw a rocket?') rather than waiting for menu selection. Frequently expresses tiredness via guessing mode. Responds positively to expanded activity options and specific, interest-based prompts.",
  "Safety & Concerns: (1) Expressed fear multiple times and seeks home/safety when scared (trigger unidentified—remain alert and reassuring). (2) Lost hat at school (confirmed April 9); shows persistence in communicating about it. (3) April 13: Expressed frustration and pressed 'Scissors' three times in succession—may indicate scissors-related incident at school or home. Monitor for clarification and continue offering reassurance and specific activities when frustrated.",
  "Session Pattern (April 10-13): Early sessions showed menu cycling (Interact → Feelings → Home) without committing to activities. Recent sessions show significant improvement: Gal is now engaging in sustained multi-turn conversations about space concepts (Stars, Planets, Rockets), selecting Drawing when offered creative expression options, and responding positively to specific activity suggestions. Demonstrates focused interest and ability to follow conceptual discussions. This shift indicates growing engagement and commitment to activities rather than menu exploration.",
  "Current Session (April 13): Gal navigated Interact → Space → Feelings, selected Happy twice, then requested more options and selected Robot. This session demonstrates: (1) Gal is engaging with specific interests (Space, Robot programming), (2) continuing pattern of emotional check-ins (Happy selections), and (3) responding positively to expanded activity options. Gal is showing improved commitment to activities rather than menu cycling. Continue offering specific, interest-based prompts and monitor for sustained engagement with hands-on activities.",
  "Current Session (April 13, 3:38 PM): Gal engaged in focused exploration of space topics. Session flow: Interact → Space (pressed twice) → Stars, Planets → Back → Space menu. Demonstrates sustained interest in space concepts and ability to navigate menus with intention. Pattern shows Gal is committing to specific topics rather than cycling aimlessly. No frustration or fear expressed this session. Continues to show strong engagement with space-related interests."
]
